# This repo is authored on Windows and runs on Linux. A shell script with CRLF
# line endings fails outright there - `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M` -
# and the same applies to the inline `run:` blocks in the workflows. Normalising
# in the repo means the platform you happened to write on cannot break the
# platform you deploy to.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.tf    text eol=lf
*.tftpl text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binaries must never go through line-ending conversion - `text=auto` usually
# detects them, but saying so explicitly costs nothing and a corrupted PDF is a
# silent failure.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary

# Benchmark inputs ship exactly as published by LogHub; the recorded results
# depend on parsing them byte-for-byte.
data/** -text
